p.src:
For macroscopic $N$, Stirling’s formula gives $N!\simeq N^Ne^{-N}\sqrt{2\pi N}.$ Keeping only the leading exponential dependence and defining $\rho=N/V$, $\frac{V^N}{N!}
 \simeq
 \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi N}}
 \left(\frac{e}{\rho}\right)^N.$ This is the lecture’s neat density reorganization. The square-root factor is subleading in $\log Z_N$, but it is displayed here rather than silently dropped.

